Description: antinomie: record AArch32 programs on arm64 by the arm table
 An arm64 kernel with CONFIG_COMPAT runs AArch32 (arm EABI) programs,
 the shape most Linux IoT samples have. Their calls were recorded with
 their numbers only (ANT_ABI_NONE): no names, no arguments decoded and
 nothing captured.
 .
 They are now recorded as ANT_ABI_COMPAT (3, already in ARCH_INFO's ABI
 mask definition) with the arm EABI table generated from
 arch/arm/tools/syscall.tbl (<asm/antinomie_compat_syscalls.h>, the
 guest copy of protocol/arm/native-syscalls.json): a 64-bit argument
 takes an aligned register pair, so each record's arguments are the
 call's registers, their low halves, with the 32-bit signed ones
 sign-extended as a native call's are.
 .
 A call that is a native call with the same arguments and objects of
 one layout on ILP32 and LP64 (strings, bytes, 32-bit and fixed-width
 values, sockaddr, time64 values; the generated ant_compat_natives
 table names 234 of them) is captured by the native code under the
 native number, while its records keep the arm number and ABI. execve
 and execveat read their vectors as 32-bit pointers (arm "pointer"
 layouts). prctl has no native counterpart (some options read arch-sized
 objects), but its options whose objects have one layout (the task name
 of PR_SET_NAME and PR_GET_NAME, int results, an anonymous mapping's
 name) are captured by the native code too. Every other call has its
 path strings captured and its other pointers recorded by address.
 Process cores of AArch32 programs are still not written.
 .
 Everything is compiled only where the architecture defines
 ANT_ABI_COMPAT (arm64 with CONFIG_COMPAT): x86-64 is unchanged.
Author: MikiMiku <jonathanirvinjo@gmail.com>
Origin: project
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-01

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/include/asm/antinomie.h b/arch/arm64/include/asm/antinomie.h
index f06382085..6833fff82 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/include/asm/antinomie.h
+++ b/arch/arm64/include/asm/antinomie.h
@@ -28,19 +28,29 @@
  * width of user virtual addresses (52 only with LVA/LPA2 and a 52-bit
  * configuration; read from TCR_EL1 then).
  */
+#ifdef CONFIG_COMPAT
+/* AArch32 programs' calls: arm EABI numbers, described by
+ * <asm/antinomie_compat_syscalls.h> (protocol/arm/native-syscalls.json).
+ */
+#define ANT_ABI_COMPAT 3
+#define ANT_ARCH_ABI_MASK (BIT(ANT_ABI_NATIVE) | BIT(ANT_ABI_COMPAT))
+#else
 #define ANT_ARCH_ABI_MASK BIT(ANT_ABI_NATIVE)
+#endif
 #define ANT_ARCH_USER_VA_BITS ((u32)vabits_actual)
 
-/* The ABI of the system call being entered, the abi field of its records. An
- * AArch32 task's calls are recorded with their number and no table.
- */
+/* The ABI of the system call being entered, the abi field of its records. */
 static __always_inline u16 ant_arch_syscall_abi(long nr)
 {
-	return test_thread_flag(TIF_32BIT) ? ANT_ABI_NONE : ANT_ABI_NATIVE;
+#ifdef ANT_ABI_COMPAT
+	if (test_thread_flag(TIF_32BIT))
+		return ANT_ABI_COMPAT;
+#endif
+	return ANT_ABI_NATIVE;
 }
 
 /* The current task is an AArch32 program: the process-core writer and its
- * readers handle native 64-bit processes only.
+ * readers handle native 64-bit processes only (ELF32 cores are not written).
  */
 static __always_inline bool ant_arch_compat_task(void)
 {
